}
```

## Accuracy Thresholds

### Primary metric: SPOT-CHECK accuracy (the real number)
- **Spot-check ≥ 85%**: Gate auto-opens after fixes + regression passes
- **Spot-check 75-84%**: Gate stays CLOSED until fixes verified AND regression passes
- **Spot-check < 75%**: Gate stays CLOSED — escalate to user before proceeding
- **Spot-check size**: 20 games per batch (minimum)
- **Aspiration**: >90% spot-check accuracy on all dimensions

### Secondary metric: regression adjusted% (heuristic estimate, not ground truth)
- **theme**: ≥97% adjusted
- **characters**: ≥95% adjusted
- **elements**: ≥95% adjusted
- **color_tone**: ≥95% adjusted
- **overall**: ≥95% adjusted
- ⚠ Adjusted% uses heuristic keyword matching — it overestimates real accuracy. Never report adjusted% as "accuracy" without the spot-check number alongside it.

### Health metrics (must be reported):
- **Correction dependency**: % of games needing manual corrections (target: <5%)
- **Bad screenshot rate**: % of games classified from non-gameplay images (target: <3%)
- Games with non-gameplay screenshots + `bad_screenshot_unfixable` are excluded from regression

## What Agents CANNOT Do

- There is no `--force-gate` flag
- Deleting `batch_gate.json` does NOT open the gate (missing file = closed)
- Setting `gate_open` without `fixes_applied: true` will not auto-open via regression
- Running batches of 11+ games without an open gate will `sys.exit(1)`
